{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1191174-psiad\u2019s-potential","id":1191174,"title":"Psiad\u2019s potential.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: \u00c6on"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-02T17:25:15-08:00","id":1191174,"title":"Psiad\u2019s potential.","content":"Are Psiads assumes to just start weaker but more general then Psions, or are they truly limited from being strong in multiple areas?<br /> <br /> Are Psiads comparable to Mesmers? Or are Psiads completely different an a new evolution?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T17:45:45-08:00","id":1191179,"title":"","content":"Psiads are the true equivalent of Novas, being the natural users of subquatum, that is noetic, energy. They are updated Mesmerist Inspired. <br /> <br /> The issue is that human genetic isn't advanced enough to make widespread Psiad awakenings possible. Hence the Doyen doing there manipulations. <br /> <br /> They are set up to have broadness rather then depth. So they can access all Aptitudes, but are restricted in how high a mode they can get. <br /> <br /> Now in 1e the rules for them were in the Aberrant line, not Trinity, and so are a little misguided, though intriguing. <br /> <br /> Also in 1e they couldn't take Quantakinetics and had to choose a category of Apptitude, both elements I hope are dropped in 2e. <br /> <br /> I hope this helps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T22:16:19-08:00","id":1191252,"title":"","content":"Well... we know that the Quantakinetic Proxy in 2E would have been able to develop all 8 Aptitudes had the Doyen not used their psychic surgery to effectively castrate her development. True, her psychic potential was enhanced by both the original Hammersmith event and the noetic device she set off as well, but chances are that she would have become the first and most powerful Psiad had the Doyen not taken any action. Would there have been more? Possibly.<br /> <br /> Now what does this mean for Psiads in general? Probably not much to be honest. Proxy Bhurano was unique, even compared to her fellow Proxies, and while she would likely have developed her psychic powers without the help of the Doyen, it is hard to say how much she would have been like other Psiads that might follow.<br /> <br /> Will Psiads be able to develop Quantakinetic powers in 2E? Probably since we have rules for Quantakinetic Psions now (though it will likely require the same prerequisite... Psi 3 to develop this or Teleportation powers). Will Psiads be able to reach Tier 3 levels of power? Again, this seems likely as we have rules for progressing to that level for Psions (though whether the same rules apply to Psiads remains to be seen). It also seems likely that Psiads will be able to develop all 8 aptitudes, possibly all the way to 5 dots (though doing so is likely to take some time). I would be willing to bet that Psiads will only be able to get the 6th or 7th dot for a single aptitude, even if they have mastered other aptitudes to the degree that would allow them to get more powers at this level. Perhaps, if they ever cross the threshold to Tier 4 levels of power they might be master more aptitudes at this level, but even this is speculation. Will Psiads favor a particular aptitude at all? Hard to say, but my gut says no as it seems like it was one of the ways that the Doyen sought to limit the growth potential of humans in mastering noetic energy. This means it will take even longer for a Psiad to develop the same level of power as a Psion even if they focus their efforts to the same degree (making them appear weaker initially, until one sees that they have no other hard limits on what they can learn... mastering on the other hand is another subject entirely).<br /> <br /> Okay, I think I am starting to ramble on now, so I should probably stop here. As a final note, I don't think that the Psiads on 2E will be anything like what was shown in 1e... they have changed a lot of the underlaying reasons for why things were done the way they were in 1e that no longer apply in 2E (such as Quantakinetics and Proxy level Psions being for STs only). It will be interesting to see what 2E Psiads look like, but chances are that any similarities they have to 1e Psiads will be cosmetic only (game mechanics-wise, they will likely be very different).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}